{"license":"DANS Licence","fileAccessRequest":true,"metadataBlocks":{"citation":{"displayName":"Citation Metadata","name":"citation","fields":[{"typeName":"title","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Teacher Report Forms (TRF) and Conners' Teacher Rating Scale ( short version - Revised ) in twins and siblings registered with the Netherlands Twin Registry (NTR)"},{"typeName":"otherId","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"otherIdAgency":{"typeName":"otherIdAgency","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"DANS-KNAW"},"otherIdValue":{"typeName":"otherIdValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"easy-dataset:61181"}}]},{"typeName":"author","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"D.I. Boomsma"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Netherlands Twin Register, dept Biological Psychology , Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"DAI"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"info:eu-repo\/dai\/nl\/323259715"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"M. Bartels"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Netherlands Twin Register, dept Biological Psychology , Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"DAI"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"info:eu-repo\/dai\/nl\/24419968X"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"J.C.N. de Geus"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Netherlands Twin Register, dept Biological Psychology \/EMGO Institute for Health & Care Research (EMGO+), Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"DAI"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"info:eu-repo\/dai\/nl\/32325957X"}},{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"C.E.M. van Beijsterveldt"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Netherlands Twin Register, dept Biological Psychology , Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"DAI"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"info:eu-repo\/dai\/nl\/147636116"}}]},{"typeName":"datasetContact","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"datasetContactName":{"typeName":"datasetContactName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"L. Ligthart"},"datasetContactAffiliation":{"typeName":"datasetContactAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"VU university"}},{"datasetContactName":{"typeName":"datasetContactName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"L. Ligthart"},"datasetContactAffiliation":{"typeName":"datasetContactAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"VU university"}}]},{"typeName":"dsDescription","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>The data were collected between 1999 and 2013 as part of the Netherlands Twin Register (NTR)'s annual teacher survey. The data collection for  the teacher surveys is ongoing and each year, the parents of children that are approximately 7, 9 (before 2009 10 years old) and 12 years old are contacted to ask for their permission to approach the teacher(s) of their children.<\/p><p>The survey for the primary school teachers includes limited information on the teacher, class and school, items on adaptive functioning of the child at school, the Teacher report Form (TRF)  (Achenbach, 2009; Verhulst & van der Ende, 2004) and the short version of the Conners’ Teacher Ratings Scale - Revised (CTRS-R) (Conners et al., 1998; Conners, 2001).<\/p><p>The survey data are stored in harmonized databases organized by age at the time of data collection. Since the CTRS-R data was collected separately from the rest of the teacher survey until 2006, it is stored in a separate database.<\/p><p>In EASY, the databases from for the different age versions of TRF and CTRS-R can be linked through anonymous identification numbers. Please consult the data manual (DocumentationDataCollectionTRF_NTR.pdf) for more information about the data collection and the relationships between the datasets from the NTR teacher survey<\/p>"}}]},{"typeName":"subject","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Social Sciences"]},{"typeName":"keyword","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"TRF"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Conners’"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"school performance"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"classroom behavior"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"twins"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"siblings"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"children"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"youth"}}]},{"typeName":"notesText","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"The depositor deposited .por files. DANS has converted these into .sav and .dta files."},{"typeName":"language","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["English"]},{"typeName":"productionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2013-01-01"},{"typeName":"contributor","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Main contributor: Netherlands Twin Register, dept Biological Psychology VU University"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Funding Agency:  Twin-family database for behavior genetics and genomics studies (NWO-MagW investeringsaanvraag NWO\/480-04-004)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"NWO Spinozapremie (NWO\/SPI 56-464-14192)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Individuele verschillen in schools presteren en neurocognitief functioneren in relatie tot genotype en omgevingsfactoren (NWO\/FES 056-31-001)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Longitudinal data collection from teachers of Dutch twins and their siblings (NWO-MagW\/ 481-08-011)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"NIMH 2 R56 MH058799-06 (PI JJ Hudziak)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Genetics of Mental Illness: European Research Council (ERC-230374)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Linking 